From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 07 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Hardcode zygote64 in init.rc for Vanadium compatibility

GrapheneOS Vanadium (TrichromeWebView/TrichromeChrome) only ships
64-bit native libraries. On Treble GSI devices the vendor partition
can override the ro.zygote property to select a 32-bit primary or
dual-arch zygote, which prevents WebView from loading and crashes
Google Play Services (and any app that uses WebView).

Hardcode the zygote64 init script import instead of relying on the
ro.zygote property. This is immune to vendor property overrides and
ensures the 64-bit only zygote is always used regardless of what the
OEM vendor image specifies.
---
 rootdir/init.rc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rootdir/init.rc b/rootdir/init.rc
--- a/rootdir/init.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.rc
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 import /init.${ro.hardware}.rc
 import /vendor/etc/init/hw/init.${ro.hardware}.rc
 import /system/etc/init/hw/init.usb.configfs.rc
-import /system/etc/init/hw/init.${ro.zygote}.rc
+import /system/etc/init/hw/init.zygote64.rc
 
 # Cgroups are mounted right before early-init using list from /etc/cgroups.json
 on early-init
